<%- include('partials/top') %>
<section class="hero">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">For CSR teams and NGOs in India</p>
    <h1>CSR money that reaches the ground — <em>and proves it.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Companies publish CSR programs. Verified NGOs apply with milestone plans. Funds are released one milestone at a time, against evidence — and your compliance report writes itself.</p>
    <div class="cta">
      <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/register?role=company">I fund CSR programs</a>
      <a class="btn btn-lg btn-ghost" href="/register?role=ngo">I run an NGO</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <dl class="stats">
    <div><dt>Verified NGOs</dt><dd><%= stats.ngos %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Open programs</dt><dd><%= stats.programs %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Released to date</dt><dd><%= inr(stats.released) %></dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="steps">
  <div class="step"><span>1</span><h3>Verify</h3><p>NGOs submit CSR-1, 12A, 80G and PAN details. Our team verifies them before any money can move.</p></div>
  <div class="step"><span>2</span><h3>Match</h3><p>Programs are ranked for each NGO by cause, geography and delivery track record — and proposals are ranked the same way for companies.</p></div>
  <div class="step"><span>3</span><h3>Commit</h3><p>Approving a proposal commits budget atomically, so a program can never be promised more than it has.</p></div>
  <div class="step"><span>4</span><h3>Release</h3><p>Each tranche is released only after the company reviews evidence for that milestone, in order.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="card demo">
  <h3>Trying the demo?</h3>
